",
  "nativeAv": "<h1 id="audio-and-video-embed">Audio and Video Embed</h1>
<p>Native audio and video embeds are opt-in and render to <code>&lt;audio&gt;</code> / <code>&lt;video&gt;</code>,
not third-party iframes.</p>
<pre><code class="language-ts">import { oxContent } from &quot;@ox-content/vite-plugin&quot;;

export default {
  plugins: [
    oxContent({
      embeds: {
        audio: true,
        video: true,
      },
    }),
  ],
};
</code></pre>
<pre><code class="language-html">&lt;audio src=&quot;https://cdn.example.com/intro.mp3&quot; title=&quot;Intro&quot; transcript=&quot;/intro.txt&quot;&gt;&lt;/audio&gt;
&lt;video src=&quot;/talk.mp4&quot; poster=&quot;/talk.jpg&quot; captions=&quot;/talk.en.vtt&quot; width=&quot;1280&quot; height=&quot;720&quot;&gt;&lt;/video&gt;
</code></pre>
<p><code>src</code> (or <code>url</code> / <code>href</code>) must be HTTPS or a same-origin relative path.
<code>javascript:</code>, <code>data:</code>, <code>http:</code>, and <code>//host/...</code> sources are rejected and left
as authored markup. Video accepts <code>poster</code>, <code>captions</code> / nested <code>&lt;track&gt;</code>,
<code>title</code>, <code>transcript</code>, <code>download</code>, and <code>width</code> / <code>height</code> for aspect-ratio
reservation. Native controls stay labeled.</p>
",
  "speakerDeck": "<h1 id="speaker-deck-embed">Speaker Deck Embed</h1>
<p>Speaker Deck embeds are opt-in. A player URL or oEmbed-resolved share URL
renders title, author, and a lazy iframe. Fetch or parse failures become a
safe link card.</p>
<pre><code class="language-ts">import { oxContent } from "@ox-content/vite-plugin";

export default {
  plugins: [
    oxContent({
      embeds: {
        speakerDeck: true,
      },
    }),
  ],
};
</code></pre>
<p>Resolved player URL (no network request):</p>
<pre><code class="language-html">&#x3C;SpeakerDeck
  url="https://speakerdeck.com/jane/my-talk"
  title="My Talk"
  author="Jane Doe"
>&#x3C;/SpeakerDeck>
</code></pre>
<a class="ox-speaker-deck ox-speaker-deck--fallback" href="https://speakerdeck.com/jane/my-talk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="ox-speaker-deck__title">My Talk</span><span class="ox-speaker-deck__author">Jane Doe</span></a>
<p>Share URLs (<code>https://speakerdeck.com/{user}/{slug}</code>) fetch oEmbed metadata at
build time and inject the player id, title, and author. <code>javascript:</code> and
<code>data:</code> URLs are rejected and stay as authored markup.</p>
<p>The iframe is lazy-loaded with <code>sandbox</code> and
<code>referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin"</code>. Pages that set a
Content-Security-Policy need <code>frame-src https://speakerdeck.com</code>.</p>
",
  "stackBlitz": "<h1 id="stackblitz-embed">StackBlitz Embed</h1>
<p>StackBlitz embeds are opt-in through the built-in embed options.</p>
<pre><code class="language-ts">import { oxContent } from "@ox-content/vite-plugin";

export default {
  plugins: [
    oxContent({
      embeds: {
        stackBlitz: true,
      },
    }),
  ],
};
</code></pre>
<pre><code class="language-html">&#x3C;StackBlitz url="https://stackblitz.com/edit/vitejs-vite" />
</code></pre>
<p>The transform appends <code>embed=1</code> and renders a sandboxed iframe.</p>
<iframe class="ox-stackblitz" src="https://stackblitz.com/edit/vitejs-vite?embed=1" title="StackBlitz project" width="100%" height="480" loading="lazy" allow="accelerometer; ambient-light-sensor; camera; encrypted-media; geolocation; gyroscope; hid; microphone; midi; payment; serial; usb; vr; xr-spatial-tracking; clipboard-read; clipboard-write; fullscreen" sandbox="allow-forms allow-modals allow-popups allow-presentation allow-same-origin allow-scripts"></iframe>
",
}
`;
